{
  "reference": "4600 WHEELER ROAD — PRELIMINARY SUBDIVISION CONCEPT. Zone RSF-95, SE-1796. Parcel 366579, GIS 230995 sq ft, recorded 5.115479 ac. PRELIMINARY. Outer boundary from the Prince George's County parcel layer (PGAtlas Property/MapServer/15), compiled from tax maps — NOT a boundary survey and NOT a plat of record. Lot lines and streets are PROPOSED by Kealee. A Maryland licensed surveyor must establish the boundary before any plat is prepared.",
  "citation": "PRELIMINARY CONCEPT — NO PLAT OF RECORD",
  "notes": [
    "This drawing is a preliminary subdivision concept. It is not a plat, not a boundary survey, and not for recording.",
    "Street layout follows the 2023 \"Wheeler Rd Subdivision Layout\" sheet for this parcel (street a tier in from the north and east boundaries, lots both sides) with ONE entrance from Wheeler Road; the second entrance and the private alley on that sheet are omitted and the far end is finished as a cul-de-sac.",
    "Lot lines are proposed to meet Sec. 27-4202 RSF-95: minimum net lot area 9500 sq ft, minimum lot width 75 ft, minimum frontage 50 ft, maximum density 4.58 du/ac of net tract area.",
    "All lots take access from the proposed street. No lot takes access from WHEELER; lots backing onto it are double-frontage lots and a no-access reservation along WHEELER is anticipated at platting.",
    "Boundary shown from the county parcel layer (Level 1). A field survey by a Maryland licensed surveyor governs.",
    "Recorded acreage 5.115479 ac (222830 sq ft) differs from the county GIS polygon (230995 sq ft) by 8165 sq ft. Both are reported; neither is adjusted. The survey resolves it.",
    "Special exception SE-1796 is of record on this property. Its conditions have not been read into this concept and govern where they conflict.",
    "PARCEL A does not front the proposed street in this layout; a 20-ft access and maintenance easement across the adjoining lot is required at platting.",
    "Stormwater management by Environmental Site Design to the maximum extent practicable (Md. Stormwater Management Act of 2007; MDE Design Manual Ch. 5; PGC Sec. 32-172). Preliminary ESD volume: 54309 sq ft impervious (23.5% of the tract: 14 lots × 2000 sq ft, 21060 sq ft pavement, sidewalks), Rv = 0.2616, P_E = 1 in → ESDv = 5036 cu ft; micro-bioretention at 2 ft × n 0.4 → 6295 sq ft of practice. PARCEL A (17206 sq ft) is reserved at the low corner of the tract (corner elevations 132–188 ft NAVD88 (feet)) for the practice, its forebay and access; it is not a building lot. Hydrologic soil group(s) B/D, C, D per USDA SSURGO MD033 — P_E is to be taken from Table 5.3 for the site's group and % impervious; the 1 in used here is the Manual's floor. Rooftop disconnection and a 6-ft infiltration berm along the rear of each lot, as the 2023 layout sheet's legend shows, are credited at concept plan and reduce the parcel; infiltration feasibility depends on the Sec. 32-131 soils investigation. A stormwater management concept approval from DPIE precedes preliminary plan.",
    "Proposed public street: 60' R/W and 26' pavement per the approved Joseph Drive section (Yocum Property, DPIE 15927-2020-0). Bend radius 150' centreline and cul-de-sac radii (50' R/W, 40' pavement) are ASSUMED — that approval is a through street with R ≥ 343'. Confirm against PGC DPW&T Specifications and Standards. THIS LAYOUT USES A 100-FT CENTRELINE RADIUS at its bends, below the 150 ft assumed above; confirm against the DPW&T minimum for a local street before preliminary plan. Street dedication 44407 sq ft. Storm drainage, sanitary sewer capacity, street lighting and forest conservation are not designed here."
  ],
